; ===================================================================================
;         Map data
;
; Here are some notes for the sections of the map data
;
;
; General variable = used for various things such as tile collision, stairs range and treasure chest graphics 
;
; Music = ID of the music to play
;
; Map update =  list of indexes used in the 'MapUpdateJmpTbl' table; processes until $FF
;
; Map transition data = data for changing maps; used when you go past an invisible boundary (e.g. geting out of town); processes until $FFFF
;     Byte 1 = X position (divided by 16) to change map at
;     Byte 2 = Y position (divided by 16) to change map at
;     Bytes 3-4 = index of the 'XYRangeJmpTbl' table that determines that range of the X and Y position above
;     Bytes 5-6 = map ID to change to
;     Byte 7 = X position (divided by 16) of destination map
;     Byte 8 = Y position (divided by 16) of destination map
;     Byte 9 = characters' facing direction of destination map; see the variable 'Map_Start_Facing_Dir' in the constants file for more info
;     Byte 10 = characters' alignment of destination map; see the variable 'Map_Start_Char_Align' in the constants file for more info
;
; Map transition data 2 = data for changing maps; used for stairs, town and dungeon tiles; processes until $FFFF
;
; Objects = list of objects loaded in the map; processes until $FFFF
;     Bytes 1-2 = index of FieldObjectsJmpTbl
;     Byte 3 = facing direction
;     Byte 4 = dialogue index
;     Bytes 5-6 = Tile number in VRAM
;     Bytes 7-8 = X position (divided by 8)
;     Bytes 9-10 = Y position (divided by 8)
;
; Treasure chests = list of treasure chests loaded in the map; processes until $FFFF
;     Byte 1 = index to determine what treasure chest to load:
;              0 = load yellow treasure chest
;              1 = load white treasure chest (found in plants)
;     Byte 2 = determines content:
;              0 = item
;              1 = money
;     Byte 3 = flag used to determine if it's been opened or not
;     Byte 4 = content determined by index of byte 2:
;              If it's content, then the value is the ID of the item
;              if it's money, then it's meseta value divided by 100
;     Byte 5 = X position (divided by 16)
;     Byte 6 = Y position (divided by 16)
;
; Interaction Areas = Action processed through the Talk button; processes until $FFFF
;     Bytes 1-2 = X position
;     Bytes 3-4 = Y position
;     Bytes 5-6 = index of the 'XYRangeJmpTbl' table that determines that range of the X and Y position above
;     Byte 7 = event type; 0 = story; 1 = chest; 2 = temp event
;     Byte 8 = check the event flag whose type is defined by the value of byte 7 above; if flag is set, then the current interaction part won't take place
;     Byte 9 = index of the 'InteractionRoutines' offset table
;     Byte 10 = value which varies depending on where you jump in the 'InteractionRoutines' table
;
; Events = list of indexes used in the 'RunEventsJmpTbl' table; processes until $FF
;
; Palettes address = address of palette values to load in CRAM
;
; Map data manager = list of indexes used in the 'MapDataManagerJmpTbl' table; processes until $FF;
;        the table is a list of subroutines that determine, for example, when an object is loaded depending on the event flags, or
;        load some palette values specific to one map.
; ===================================================================================



; ===================================================================================
