; =========================================================================================
;                Enemy Data
;
; Byte 1-2: HP
; Byte 3: Basic attack elemental. The only elementals used for this are:
;   01: Physical (others may call this force)
;   02: Energy (others may call this radiation or laser)
;   07: Electric (others may call this lightning)
;
; Byte 4: Basic attack status effect. The only values used for this are:
;   00: nothing
;   1B: poison
;   1C: paralyze
;
;
; Byte 5: Strength
; Byte 6: Mental
; Byte 7: Agility
; Byte 8: Dexterity
; Byte 9-10: Attack
; Byte 11: Defense
; Byte 12: Magic defense
;
; Byte 13: Physical properties
;   00: immune
;   01: resistant
;   02: normal
;   03: weak
;   04: very weak
;
; Byte 14: Energy properties
; Byte 15: Fire properties
; Byte 16: Gravity properties
; Byte 17: Water properties
; Byte 18: Anti-Evil properties
; Byte 19: Electric properties
; Byte 20: Holyword properties
; Byte 21: Brose properties
; Byte 22: Biological properties
; Byte 23: Psychic properties
; Byte 24: Mechanical properties
; Byte 25: Efess properties
; Byte 26: Destroy properties
;
; Byte 27: Always 0
; Byte 28: Always 0
;
; Byte 29: AI instruction 1
; Byte 30: AI instruction 2
; Byte 31: AI instruction 3
; Byte 32: AI instruction 4
;   The values for these bytes are as follows:
;   01 - If adjacent to empty space
;   02 - If at 50% or less HP
;   03 - If adjacent to Wiredine
;   04 - If adjacent to Arthropod
;   05 - If C-Ray Tube is adjacent to two Sat.Minions
;   06 - If adjacent to Zol Slug
;   07 - If attacked physically
;   08 - If attacked magically
;   09 - If alone
;   0A - If attacked with techs
;   0B - If surprise attack on player
;   0C - If tech sealed
;   0D - If adjacent to Hakenleft
;   0E - If adjacent to Bladeright
;   0F - If anyone is damaged
;   10 - unused
;   11 - If at 25% or less HP
;   12 - If there are three Xe-A-Thouls
;   13 - Psyco-wanded Zio (Nightmare) - could be "if Nightmare not used"
;
;
; Byte 33: Ability 1, used when instruction 1 is satisfied
; Byte 34: Ability 2, used when instruction 2 is satisfied
; Byte 35: Ability 3, used when instruction 3 is satisfied
; Byte 36: Ability 4, used when instruction 4 is satisfied
;
; Byte 37: Ability 5 (regular)
; Byte 38: Ability 6
; Byte 39: Ability 7
; Byte 40: Ability 8
; Byte 41: Ability 9
; Byte 42: Ability 10
; Byte 43: Ability 11
; Byte 44: Ability 12
;
; Byte 45-46: Experience
; Byte 47-48: Meseta
; =========================================================================================
