; =========================================================================================
;                Inventory Data
;
; Byte 1: Effect
;   1: damage
;   2: death
;   3: attack down
;	4: defense down
;   6: agility down
;   7: sleep
;   8: silence, as the player Seals technique
;   9: attack up
;   $A: defense up
;   $B: magic defense up
;   $C: agility up
;	$D = element resistance up
;	$E = wake up
;   $12: heal HP
;	$13: cure poison
;	$14: cure paralysis
;	$15: revive character
;	$16: full healing
;   $1B: poison
;   $1C: paralyze
;   $1D: android death
;   $21: dexterity down
;   $26: dexterity up
;   $27: restore stats
;   $2B: increase stats by 20
;
; Byte 2: Power
;
; Byte 3: Target (lower nybble)
;   1: Single enemy
;   2: All enemies
;   3: Self
;   4: Single character (humans)
;	5: All characters (humans)
;	6: Single character (androids)
;	7: All characters (androids)
;   8: Single character
;   9: All characters

; Byte 4: Hit chance; not applicable if byte 5 is 0 or for effects such as damage and healing

; Byte 5: Determines which stat to use as resistance for targets
;   1: strength
;   2: mental
;   3: agility
;   4: dexterity
;   5: attack
;   6: defense
;   7: magic defense
;
; Byte 6: Element (mainly used for status effects)
;   1: Physical
;   2: Energy
;   3: Fire
;   4: Gravity
;   5: Water/Ice
;   6: Anti-Evil/Holy
;   7: Lightning
;   8: Holyword
;   9: Brose
;   $A: Biological
;   $B: Psychic
;   $C: Mechanical
;   $D: Efess
;   $E: Destroy
;
; Byte 7: Always 0.
;
; Byte 8: Affects the animation.
;
; Byte 9-10: Used-by bytes. Bitfield. If bit is set, the item can be equipped by the relative character.
;
;   bit 0: Chaz
;   bit 1: Alys
;   bit 2: Hahn
;   bit 3: Rune
;   bit 4: Gryz
;   bit 5: Rika
;   bit 6: Demi
;   bit 7: Wren
;   bit 8: Raja
;   bit 9: Kyra
;   bit 10: Seth
;
; Byte 11: Indicates "type".
;   1: 1 handed, single-target weapon
;   2: 1 handed, multi-target weapon (Slashers)
;   3: 2 handed, single-target weapon (Swords, axes, staffs, most guns)
;   4: 2 handed, multi-target weapon (Pulse guns)
;   5: Shields
;   6: Headwear and rings
;   7: Body equipment
;   8: Disposable item
;   9: Plot-related items
;   $A: Out-of-battle-only items, like decorations and vehicles
;
; Byte 12: Strength bonus
; Byte 13: Mental bonus
; Byte 14: Agility bonus
; Byte 15: Dexterity bonus
; Byte 16: Attack bonus (note that Strength bonus will be added to a character's
;   effective attack power, making this appear different on some equips)
;
; Byte 17: Defense bonus (note that Agility bonus will be added to a character's
;   effective defense, making this appear different on some equips)
;
; Byte 18: Magic defense bonus (note that Mental bonus will be added to a
;   character's effective defense, making this appear different on some equips)
;
; Byte 19: Element for attack and defense. See byte 6 for the values.
;
; Byte 20: Effect post-attack. See byte 1 for the values.
;
; Byte 21-22: Meseta cost.
; =========================================================================================
